Robin Lee Powell scripsit:

> For the same reason you can't say "pu bai klama": LALR(1).  If you
> haven't gotten used to doing "pu je bai klama", you either are new,
> or aren't interested in doing proper formal lojban anyways.

Actually "pu bai klama" is fine: it's "pu [ku] bai klama".  The
rules about tenses are really pretty nugatory: if you violate them,
the parser will just insert ku's anyhow.

Furthermore, the tense part of the grammar is not at all LALR(1).

